<item>
  <title>First Dose of COVID Vaccine</title>
  <dc:creator>synesis </dc:creator>
  <link>https://benjaminhan.net/posts/20210426-covid-vaccine-first-dose/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=feed</link>
  <description><![CDATA[<p><a href="https://benjaminhan.net/posts/20210426-covid-vaccine-first-dose/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=feed">Read on benjaminhan.net →</a></p>
 





<div class="quarto-figure quarto-figure-center">
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://benjaminhan.net/posts/20210426-covid-vaccine-first-dose/cover.jpg" class="img-fluid figure-img"></p>
<figcaption>COVID vaccine first dose. Image from <a href="https://berthub.eu/articles/posts/reverse-engineering-source-code-of-the-biontech-pfizer-vaccine/">berthub.eu</a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
<p>Very proud to have received my first dose of COVID vaccine today. How incredibly lucky and privileged I am to be living in this time and benefiting from this scientific miracle, an mRNA-based vaccine developed within a record time!</p>
<p>So many things had to happen before this moment to make it real: the long string of scientific ingenuities, the bravery of immigrants, a place where merits and innovations are still rewarded regardless of race, color, religion, and national origin, the persistent pursuit for a scientific dream, the personal sacrifices and perseverance, and the incredibly disciplined teamwork - all of these ingredients to make up this little dose of medicine just in time!</p>
<ul>
<li>Reverse engineering Pfizer vaccine: <a href="https://berthub.eu/articles/posts/reverse-engineering-source-code-of-the-biontech-pfizer-vaccine/" class="uri">https://berthub.eu/articles/posts/reverse-engineering-source-code-of-the-biontech-pfizer-vaccine/</a></li>
<li>The scientist behind the mRNA-based vaccines - Katalin Karikó: <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/08/health/coronavirus-mrna-kariko.html" class="uri">https://www.nytimes.com/2021/04/08/health/coronavirus-mrna-kariko.html</a></li>
<li>How Pfizer makes its Covid-19 vaccine: <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/health/pfizer-coronavirus-vaccine.html" class="uri">https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/health/pfizer-coronavirus-vaccine.html</a></li>
</ul>
<hr>
